<title>HONG KONG: HK GDP rises 5.1 pct in 3rd quarter of 1996.</title>
<headline>HK GDP rises 5.1 pct in 3rd quarter of 1996.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department gave the following estimates of real gross domestic product growth (in percent).</p>
<p>				 3rd qtr '96  2nd qtr '96 (unrevised)</p>
<p> GDP			     5.1	    4.3</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  4.5	    2.5</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  5.3	    5.2</p>
<p>				 3rd qtr '96  2nd qtr '96 (unrevised)</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	  5.8	   10.4</p>
<p> Domestic exports:	  -9.9	   -9.0</p>
<p> Re-exports:		   8.0	    6.5</p>
<p> Exports of services:	7.1	    5.2</p>
<p>Implicit price</p>
<p> deflator of GDP:	    4.6	    6.5</p>
<p>Estimates of individual expenditure components of GDP for the 3rd quarter of 1996 were updated based on the latest data available from various sources, the government said.  </p>
<p>The following table is of revised GDP data. All figures are year-on-year at constant (1990) market prices.</p>
<p>				 1996 Q2   1996 Q1   1995 Q4   1995 Q3</p>
<p> GDP			     4.6	 3.3	 3.4	 4.2</p>
<p>Components</p>
<p>Private consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  3.3	 3.6	 0.4	 1.0</p>
<p>Government consumption</p>
<p> expenditure:		  5.2	 2.9	 5.0	 5.6</p>
<p>				 1996 Q2   1996 Q1   1995 Q4   1995 Q3</p>
<p>Gross domestic fixed</p>
<p> capital formation:	 10.1	11.5	 4.7     15.3</p>
<p> Total exports of goods    3.9	 4.9	 6.8     12.2</p>
<p> Imports of goods	    2.2	 5.2	 8.0     13.5</p>
<p> Exports of services	 5.3	 7.3	10.2     12.9</p>
<p> Imports of services	 1.3	 2.4	 4.6	5.4</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
